    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **284 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing/reuse behavior in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- In `addOwner`, added `owner.setCity(resolveCity(owner.getCity()))` before the customer code / membership number is assigned, so the resolved spelling is what gets stored and returned in the `city` field.\n- Added `resolveCity(String)`: if any existing owner already lives in that city (matched case- and whitespace-insensitively via the existing `normalize` helper), it reuses that owner's exact city spelling; otherwise it title-cases the supplied value.\n- Added `toTitleCase(String)`: upper-cases the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest, preserving original whitespace (e.g. `\"new york\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`).\n\nBecause the customer-code generation already upper-cases the city independently, that behavior is unaffected.\n\n**Tests added** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`):\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesCityForNewCity` \u2014 `\"sPRINGfield\"` \u2192 `\"Springfield\"`.\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesMultiWordCity` \u2014 `\"new york\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling` \u2014 `\"MADISON\"` reuses seed spelling `\"Madison\"`.",
